@@ -1,1 +1,10 @@
+
+### Blender node-link lifetime and repeated execution
+
+- A `NodeLink` becomes invalid immediately after `links.remove(link)`.
+  Do not read `link.to_node`, `link.to_socket`, or other fields afterward.
+  Use mutually exclusive `if`/`elif` branches or `continue` after removal.
+- Generated part constructors must run repeatedly in the same Blender scene,
+  because part checks, assembly, and final export reuse materials and nodes.
+  Test material cleanup with existing links, not only on the first creation.
